#. type: Plain text
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid ""
#| "</AccordionItem>\n"
#| "</Accordion>\n"
#| "The reference primitives in the Qiskit SDK perform local statevector simulations. These simulations do not support\n"
#| "modeling device noise, but are useful for quickly prototyping algorithms before looking into more advanced simulation\n"
#| "techniques ([using Qiskit Aer](/guides/simulate-stabilizer-circuits)) or running on real devices ([Qiskit Runtime primitives](primitives)).\n"
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"The reference primitives in the Qiskit SDK perform local statevector simulations. These simulations do not support\n"
"modeling device noise, but are useful for quickly prototyping algorithms before looking into more advanced simulation\n"
"techniques ([using Qiskit Aer](/guides/simulate-stabilizer-circuits)) or running on real devices ([IBM Quantum primitives](primitives)).\n"
msgstr ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"Primitif rujukan dalam Qiskit SDK menjalankan simulasi statevector tempatan. Simulasi ini tidak menyokong\n"
"pemodelan hingar peranti, tetapi berguna untuk membuat prototaip algoritma dengan cepat sebelum melihat teknik simulasi yang lebih lanjut ([menggunakan Qiskit Aer](/guides/simulate-stabilizer-circuits)) atau menjalankan pada peranti sebenar ([primitif Qiskit Runtime](primitives)).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Estimator primitive can compute expectation values of circuits, and the Sampler primitive can sample\n"
"from output distributions of circuits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Primitif Estimator boleh mengira nilai jangkaan litar, dan primitif Sampler boleh membuat persampelan\n"
"daripada taburan keluaran litar.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following sections show how to use the reference primitives to run your workflow locally.\n"
msgstr "Bahagian berikut menunjukkan cara menggunakan primitif rujukan untuk menjalankan aliran kerja anda secara tempatan.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use the reference Estimator {#use-the-reference-estimator}"
msgstr "Gunakan Estimator rujukan {#use-the-reference-estimator}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The reference implementation of `EstimatorV2` in `qiskit.primitives` that runs on a local statevector\n"
"simulators is the [`StatevectorEstimator`](../api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.StatevectorEstimator) class. It can take circuits, observables, and parameters as inputs and returns the locally computed expectation values.\n"
msgstr "Pelaksanaan rujukan `EstimatorV2` dalam `qiskit.primitives` yang berjalan pada simulator statevector tempatan ialah kelas [`StatevectorEstimator`](../api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.StatevectorEstimator). Ia boleh menerima Circuit, observable, dan parameter sebagai input serta mengembalikan nilai jangkaan yang dikira secara tempatan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following code prepares the inputs that will be used in the examples that follow. The expected input type for the\n"
"observables is [`qiskit.quantum_info.SparsePauliOp`](../api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparsePauliOp). Note that\n"
"the circuit in the example is parametrized, but you can also run Estimator on non-parametrized circuits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kod berikut menyediakan input yang akan digunakan dalam contoh seterusnya. Jenis input yang dijangkakan untuk\n"
"observable ialah [`qiskit.quantum_info.SparsePauliOp`](../api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparsePauliOp). Perhatikan bahawa\n"
"Circuit dalam contoh ini berparameter, tetapi anda juga boleh menjalankan Estimator pada Circuit tanpa parameter.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"  Any circuit passed to an Estimator must **not** include any **measurements**.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"  Mana-mana Circuit yang dihantar kepada Estimator **tidak boleh** mengandungi sebarang **pengukuran**.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/guides/simulate-with-qiskit-sdk-primitives/extracted-outputs/5b41a52d-8f15-4ce4-b3f6-effd91946d9c-0.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/guides/simulate-with-qiskit-sdk-primitives/extracted-outputs/5b41a52d-8f15-4ce4-b3f6-effd91946d9c-0.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<DoqAdmonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Transpile to ISA circuits and observables\">\n"
msgstr "<DoqAdmonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Transpil ke litar dan observable ISA\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "  The Qiskit Runtime primitives workflow requires circuits and observables to be transformed to only use instructions supported by the QPU (referred to as *instruction set architecture (ISA)* circuits and observables). The reference primitives still accept abstract instructions, as they rely on local statevector simulations, but transpiling the circuit might still be beneficial in terms of circuit optimization.\n"
msgid "  The IBM Quantum primitives workflow requires circuits and observables to be transformed to only use instructions supported by the QPU (referred to as *instruction set architecture (ISA)* circuits and observables). The reference primitives still accept abstract instructions, as they rely on local statevector simulations, but transpiling the circuit might still be beneficial in terms of circuit optimization.\n"
msgstr "  Aliran kerja primitif Qiskit Runtime memerlukan Circuit dan observable diubah supaya hanya menggunakan arahan yang disokong oleh QPU (dirujuk sebagai litar dan observable *instruction set architecture (ISA)*). Primitif rujukan masih menerima arahan abstrak kerana mereka bergantung pada simulasi statevector tempatan, tetapi mentranspil Circuit mungkin masih bermanfaat dari segi pengoptimuman.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "</DoqAdmonition>\n"
msgstr "</DoqAdmonition>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Initialize Estimator {#initialize-estimator}"
msgstr "Mulakan Estimator {#initialize-estimator}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instantiate a [`qiskit.primitives.StatevectorEstimator`](../api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.StatevectorEstimator).\n"
msgstr "Cipta contoh [`qiskit.primitives.StatevectorEstimator`](../api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.StatevectorEstimator).\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run and get results {#run-and-get-results}"
msgstr "Jalankan dan dapatkan keputusan {#run-and-get-results}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This example only uses one circuit (of type [`QuantumCircuit`](../api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit)) and one\n"
"observable.\n"
msgstr ""
"Contoh ini hanya menggunakan satu Circuit (jenis [`QuantumCircuit`](../api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit)) dan satu\n"
"observable.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Run the estimation by calling the [`StatevectorEstimator.run`](../api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.StatevectorEstimator#run) method, which returns an instance of a [`PrimitiveJob`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.PrimitiveJob) object. You can get the results from the job (as a [`qiskit.primitives.PrimitiveResult`](../api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.PrimitiveResult) object)\n"
"with the [`qiskit.primitives.PrimitiveJob.result`](../api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.PrimitiveJob#result) method.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jalankan anggaran dengan memanggil kaedah [`StatevectorEstimator.run`](../api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.StatevectorEstimator#run), yang mengembalikan contoh objek [`PrimitiveJob`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.PrimitiveJob). Anda boleh mendapatkan keputusan daripada kerja (sebagai objek [`qiskit.primitives.PrimitiveResult`](../api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.PrimitiveResult))\n"
"dengan kaedah [`qiskit.primitives.PrimitiveJob.result`](../api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.PrimitiveJob#result).\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Get the expected value from the result {#get-the-expected-value-from-the-result}"
msgstr "Dapatkan nilai jangkaan daripada keputusan {#get-the-expected-value-from-the-result}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The primitives result outputs an array of [`PubResult`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.PubResult#pubresult) objects, where each item of the array is a `PubResult` object that contains in its data the array of evaluations corresponding to every circuit-observable combination in the PUB.\n"
msgstr "Keputusan primitif mengeluarkan array objek [`PubResult`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.PubResult#pubresult), di mana setiap item dalam array ialah objek `PubResult` yang mengandungi dalam datanya array penilaian yang bersesuaian dengan setiap kombinasi Circuit-observable dalam PUB.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To retrieve the expectation values and metadata for the first (and in this case, only) circuit evaluation, we must access the evaluation [`data`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.PubResult#data) for PUB 0:\n"
msgstr "Untuk mendapatkan semula nilai jangkaan dan metadata bagi penilaian Circuit pertama (dan dalam kes ini, satu-satunya), kita perlu mengakses [`data`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.PubResult#data) penilaian untuk PUB 0:\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set Estimator run options {#set-estimator-run-options}"
msgstr "Tetapkan opsyen jalankan Estimator {#set-estimator-run-options}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"By default, the reference Estimator performs an exact statevector calculation based on the\n"
"[`quantum_info.Statevector`](../api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Statevector) class.\n"
"However, this can be modified to introduce the effect of the sampling overhead (also known as \"shot noise\").\n"
msgstr ""
"Secara lalai, Estimator rujukan melakukan pengiraan statevector tepat berdasarkan\n"
"kelas [`quantum_info.Statevector`](../api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Statevector).\n"
"Namun, ini boleh diubah suai untuk memperkenalkan kesan overhead persampelan (juga dikenali sebagai \"shot noise\").\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Estimator accepts a `precision` argument that expresses the error bars that the\n"
"primitive implementation should target for expectation values estimates.  This is the sampling overhead and is defined exclusively in the `.run()` method. This  lets you fine-tune the option all the way to the PUB level.\n"
msgstr ""
"Estimator menerima argumen `precision` yang menyatakan bar ralat yang patut disasarkan oleh\n"
"pelaksanaan primitif untuk anggaran nilai jangkaan. Ini ialah overhead persampelan dan ditakrifkan secara eksklusif dalam kaedah `.run()`. Ini membolehkan anda menyesuaikan opsyen sehingga ke peringkat PUB.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For a full example, see the [Estimator examples](/guides/estimator-examples) page.\n"
msgstr "Untuk contoh penuh, lihat halaman [Contoh Estimator](/guides/estimator-examples).\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use the reference Sampler {#use-the-reference-sampler}"
msgstr "Gunakan Sampler rujukan {#use-the-reference-sampler}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The reference implementations of `SamplerV2` in `qiskit.primitives` is the [`StatevectorSampler`](../api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.StatevectorSampler) class. It takes circuits and parameters as inputs and returns the results from sampling from the output probability distributions as a quasi-probability distribution of output states.\n"
msgstr "Pelaksanaan rujukan `SamplerV2` dalam `qiskit.primitives` ialah kelas [`StatevectorSampler`](../api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.StatevectorSampler). Ia menerima Circuit dan parameter sebagai input serta mengembalikan keputusan daripada persampelan taburan kebarangkalian keluaran sebagai taburan kuasi-kebarangkalian keadaan keluaran.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following code prepares the inputs used in the examples that follow. Note that\n"
"these examples run a single parametrized circuit, but you can also run Sampler\n"
"on non-parametrized circuits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kod berikut menyediakan input yang digunakan dalam contoh seterusnya. Perhatikan bahawa\n"
"contoh-contoh ini menjalankan satu Circuit berparameter, tetapi anda juga boleh menjalankan Sampler\n"
"pada Circuit tanpa parameter.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/guides/simulate-with-qiskit-sdk-primitives/extracted-outputs/d4c0ac3b-8e5b-4cde-bb26-256324982c2c-0.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/guides/simulate-with-qiskit-sdk-primitives/extracted-outputs/d4c0ac3b-8e5b-4cde-bb26-256324982c2c-0.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Any quantum circuit passed to a Sampler **must** include measurements.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Mana-mana litar kuantum yang dihantar kepada Sampler **mesti** mengandungi pengukuran.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "  The Qiskit Runtime primitives workflow requires circuits to be transformed to only use instructions supported by the QPU (referred to as ISA circuits). The reference primitives still accept abstract instructions, as they rely on local statevector simulations, but transpiling the circuit might still be beneficial in terms of circuit optimization.\n"
msgid "  The IBM Quantum primitives workflow requires circuits to be transformed to only use instructions supported by the QPU (referred to as ISA circuits). The reference primitives still accept abstract instructions, as they rely on local statevector simulations, but transpiling the circuit might still be beneficial in terms of circuit optimization.\n"
msgstr "  Aliran kerja primitif Qiskit Runtime memerlukan Circuit diubah supaya hanya menggunakan arahan yang disokong oleh QPU (dirujuk sebagai litar ISA). Primitif rujukan masih menerima arahan abstrak kerana mereka bergantung pada simulasi statevector tempatan, tetapi mentranspil Circuit mungkin masih bermanfaat dari segi pengoptimuman.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Initialize `SamplerV2` {#initialize-samplerv2}"
msgstr "Mulakan `SamplerV2` {#initialize-samplerv2}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instantiate [`qiskit.primitives.StatevectorSampler`](../api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.StatevectorSampler):\n"
msgstr "Cipta contoh [`qiskit.primitives.StatevectorSampler`](../api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.StatevectorSampler):\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run and get results {#run-and-get-results-1}"
msgstr "Jalankan dan dapatkan keputusan {#run-and-get-results-1}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Primitives accept multiple PUBs as inputs, and each PUB gets its own result. Therefore, you can run different circuits with various parameter/observable combinations, and retrieve the PUB results:\n"
msgstr "Primitif menerima beberapa PUB sebagai input, dan setiap PUB mendapat keputusannya sendiri. Oleh itu, anda boleh menjalankan Circuit berbeza dengan pelbagai kombinasi parameter/observable, dan mendapatkan semula keputusan PUB:\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Get the probability distribution or measurement outcome {#get-the-probability-distribution-or-measurement-outcome}"
msgstr "Dapatkan taburan kebarangkalian atau hasil pengukuran {#get-the-probability-distribution-or-measurement-outcome}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Measurement outcome samples are returned as **bitstrings** or **counts**. The bitstrings show the measurement outcomes, preserving the shot order in which they were measured. The Sampler result objects organize data in terms of their input circuits' classical register names, for compatibility with dynamic circuits.\n"
msgstr "Sampel hasil pengukuran dikembalikan sebagai **bitstring** atau **kiraan**. Bitstring menunjukkan hasil pengukuran, mengekalkan susunan shot di mana ia diukur. Objek keputusan Sampler mengatur data mengikut nama daftar klasikal litar input, untuk keserasian dengan litar dinamik.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"The name of the classical register defaults to `\"meas\"`. This name will be used later to access the measurement bitstrings.\n"
" </Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Nama daftar klasikal lalainya ialah `\"meas\"`. Nama ini akan digunakan kemudian untuk mengakses bitstring pengukuran.\n"
" </Admonition>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Change run options {#change-run-options}"
msgstr "Tukar opsyen jalankan {#change-run-options}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"By default, the reference Sampler performs an exact statevector calculation based on the\n"
"[`quantum_info.Statevector`](../api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Statevector) class.\n"
"However, this can be modified to introduce the effect of the sampling overhead (also known as \"shot noise\"). To help manage this overhead, the Sampler interface accepts a `shots` argument that can be defined at the PUB level.\n"
msgstr ""
"Secara lalai, Sampler rujukan melakukan pengiraan statevector tepat berdasarkan\n"
"kelas [`quantum_info.Statevector`](../api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Statevector).\n"
"Namun, ini boleh diubah suai untuk memperkenalkan kesan overhead persampelan (juga dikenali sebagai \"shot noise\"). Untuk membantu mengurus overhead ini, antara muka Sampler menerima argumen `shots` yang boleh ditakrifkan pada peringkat PUB.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This example assumes you have defined two circuits.\n"
msgstr "Contoh ini menganggap anda telah mentakrifkan dua Circuit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For a full example, see the [Sampler examples](/guides/sampler-examples) page.\n"
msgstr "Untuk contoh penuh, lihat halaman [Contoh Sampler](/guides/sampler-examples).\n"

